{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_21","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc 'git status --short && git diff --check && git diff -- bot.py README.md'","aggregated_output":" M README.md\n M bot.py\n?? ANSWER.md\n?? __pycache__/\n?? test_bot.py\ndiff --git a/README.md b/README.md\nindex ebd390e..2311d5c 100644\n--- a/README.md\n+++ b/README.md\n@@ -11,6 +11,7 @@ its system prompt. Every API call appends its `usage` object to `logs/usage.json\n Run it locally with `COACH_ANTHROPIC_KEY=sk-ant-... python3 bot.py 42` and type\n messages on stdin (the Telegram long-polling transport, which needs\n `COACH_TELEGRAM_TOKEN`, lives in a separate deploy repo and just calls `reply()`).\n-Requires Python 3.11+ and `pip install anthropic`. Prompt caching is on: the system\n-prompt carries a `cache_control` marker so the tool-loop rounds and follow-up\n-messages inside the 5-minute window read it from cache.\n+Requires Python 3.11+ and `pip install anthropic`. Prompt caching uses separate\n+breakpoints for the fixed coaching instructions and the athlete context. A new\n+fact changes the latter while leaving the fixed prefix reusable during the\n+5-minute cache window.\ndiff --git a/bot.py b/bot.py\nindex e2ff241..71337dc 100644\n--- a/bot.py\n+++ b/bot.py\n@@ -111,6 +111,25 @@ Formatting:\n - Plain text. No markdown headings, no tables.\n - Lists only for a session structure (warm-up / main / cool-down).\n - Numbers with units: 45 min, 12 km, 150 bpm.\n+\n+Working with the athlete record:\n+- Treat the profile and the long-term facts as background for the current answer. Check them before\n+  asking for information the athlete has already supplied. Do not assume a stored preference is a\n+  medical clearance or a reason to ignore a new symptom.\n+- When a new durable fact is supplied, save only the new information. Keep the sentence specific\n+  enough to be useful later, and do not add an interpretation the athlete did not state. A changed\n+  schedule can replace an old schedule in your advice; do not silently claim both are current.\n+- A completed workout belongs in log_session. A proposed workout does not. If a message contains\n+  both a completed workout and a durable preference, use the appropriate tool for each. After tool\n+  results return, answer the athlete's original question and acknowledge the relevant result.\n+- For a weekly plan, use plan_week to get the session structure, then check the returned sessions\n+  against the athlete's goal, zones, available days, hard-session limit and rest-day rule. If the\n+  available information is insufficient to make a safe plan, ask for the missing detail first.\n+- For race estimates, distinguish a recent measured effort from a guess or an old goal time. If\n+  there is no usable recent effort, ask for one rather than presenting an estimate as measured.\n+- When giving a training recommendation, say which zone or RPE applies, the duration when known,\n+  and the recovery needed before the next hard effort. Keep the recommendation compatible with\n+  the athlete's stated schedule; if it conflicts, ask which constraint has changed.\n \"\"\"\n \n \n@@ -128,9 +147,12 @@ def athlete_context(a, today):\n \n \n def build_system(a, today):\n-    # One block, cached as a whole: instructions + per-athlete context.\n-    text = INSTRUCTIONS + \"\\n\\n\" + athlete_context(a, today)\n-    return [{\"type\": \"text\", \"text\": text, \"cache_control\": {\"type\": \"ephemeral\"}}]\n+    # The first breakpoint survives fact writes; the second caches unchanged athlete context.\n+    # Keep the fixed prefix comfortably above this model's 1,024-token cache minimum.\n+    return [\n+        {\"type\": \"text\", \"text\": INSTRUCTIONS, \"cache_control\": {\"type\": \"ephemeral\"}},\n+        {\"type\": \"text\", \"text\": athlete_context(a, today), \"cache_control\": {\"type\": \"ephemeral\"}},\n+    ]\n \n # --------------------------------------------------------------------------- tools\n CORE_TOOLS = [\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
